# [[confused|Confused]] or [[perplexed]].
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Vanity Fair|url=http://books.google.nl/books?id=Ql0OAAAAQAAJ&printsec=frontcover&dq=vanity+fair&hl=nl&sa=X&ei=u1HrUo-zAoHs0gWq7YHYBw&ved=0CD0Q6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=vanity%20fair&f=false|11|passage=(...) when the day of the departure came, between her two customs of laughing and crying, Miss Sedley was greatly '''puzzled''' how to act.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1920|author={{w|Herman Cyril McNeile}}|title=Bulldog Drummond|chapter=1
|passage=Once or twice he scratched his head, and stared out of the window with a '''puzzled''' frown. And each time, after a brief survey of the other side of Half Moon Street, he turned back again to the breakfast table with a grin.}}

